  "body": "Currently it is not possible to manually include compressed css and js files. In highly restricted development environments it would be very helpful to include these manually compressed files.\r\nThis improvement would allow the following changes in the HTML DOM:\r\n\r\n```HTML\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n  <head>\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"C:\\local\\path\\to\\stylesheet.css.gz\">\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"C:\\local\\path\\to\\javascript.js.gz\"></script>\r\n  </head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    ...\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think this specification change should not mean any profound changes, since the HTTP protocol can handle gzip files.",
